<http://data.silknow.org/event/5e532d3b-afa0-34cb-b72d-6a6a895281bb>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Made by Mary Queen of Scots, Elizabeth, Countess of Shrewsbury and members of her household. Probably made in Sheffield Castle where Mary was imprisoned. The Oxburgh Hangings. Hanging with applied panels of embroidery, formerly at Oxburgh Hall, Norfolk. Originally all the panels were applied to a green velvet background, parts of which survive on the central panel and on several of the smaller panels."@en ;
        ecrm:P14_carried_out_by        <http://data.silknow.org/actor/d858d816-5ef4-3380-8e9e-1aff3f2527db> ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P23_transferred_title_from
                "Presented by Art Fund" ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/cdbeb7e0-3fcb-34c7-935c-4b4d090db033> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Made by Mary Queen of Scots, Elizabeth, Countess of Shrewsbury and members of her household. Probably made in Sheffield Castle where Mary was imprisoned. The Oxburgh Hangings. Hanging with applied panels of embroidery, formerly at Oxburgh Hall, Norfolk. Originally all the panels were applied to a green velvet background, parts of which survive on the central panel and on several of the smaller panels."@en .

